 "what_each_lets_a_third_party_verify": {
  "anchor_chain_alone": "the monitor's records are authentic (Ed25519 under the published key) and linked; it holds no row content, so alone it shows neither what a row said nor whether a recorder is unchanged",
  "anchor_chain_plus_recorder_or_extract": "whether each sealed segment of the presented rows reproduces the anchored root (match, violation, or unknown); a changed row is detected, its original content is not recovered",
  "anchor_chain_plus_escrow": "each escrow line is authenticated by reproducing an anchored root or keylog sub-range (counts above), after which the original committed fields of every sealed second are recoverable",
  "escrow_or_replica_alone": "self-consistency only: the replica's host (or anyone who can write it) can change a line and recompute its fold, as the doctored-line control shows; a third party must trust that host for integrity"
 },
 "what_the_anchor_host_learns": "Roots (32-byte hashes), row counts per segment, the poll's times and watermarks (row keys), and per first-observed row its key offset, a 32-bit prefix of its row hash and the second it was in (field lists above); so it learns WHEN rows were written and how many (the activity timeline, counted above), and no committed value (search above). The escrow's host holds every committed value of every sealed row."
}